## Division Highlights

### Nexus Aerospace

**Falcon X Countdown**
The Falcon X UAV program achieved a major milestone with the successful completion of ground testing. First flight is targeted for May 2026.

**Starliner Progress**
Our next-generation satellite bus completed preliminary design review. Orders now exceed $85 million.

**Award Win**
Dr. Elena Rodriguez was named "Aerospace Engineer of the Year" by Aviation Week.

### Nexus Energy Systems

**GreenHydrogen Update**
Construction is 68% complete at our El Paso facility. First hydrogen production expected March 2026.

**Desert Sun Milestone**
The Desert Sun Solar Farm reached 350 MW of generating capacity, powering over 100,000 homes.

**Shell Partnership**
We finalized a 10-year, $450 million offtake agreement with Shell for green hydrogen.

### Nexus Digital Solutions

**FedRAMP Achievement**
CyberShield achieved FedRAMP High authorization, opening the federal market.

**Customer Win**
Signed $45 million contract with major financial services firm for CyberShield deployment.

**QuantumLeap Upgrade**
Our 127-qubit quantum computer became operational, doubling our previous capacity.

### Nexus Advanced Materials

**HTS Wire Record**
Achieved record production of 500 km of superconducting wire in Q4.

**BatteryTech JV**
Finalized joint venture with Toyota for solid-state battery production.

**New Capability**
Launched advanced composites production line for aerospace applications.

